WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:05.670
Beware!

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:07.299
I've come from the future

00:00:07.299 --> 00:00:10.150
to warn you that a plague will soon

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:13.580
wipe out all originality on basic cable!

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:16.699
I explain everything on this week's episode

00:00:16.699 --> 00:00:18.430
of Angry Nerd!

00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:20.580
So the 1995 sci-fi movie

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:22.590
12 Monkeys is mutating

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:24.510
into a series on the Syfy channel.

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:25.510
“A couple of years from now,”

00:00:25.510 --> 00:00:26.510
“the entire human race will”

00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:28.360
“be wiped out be a plague….”

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:30.430
I asked you what you thought of this,

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:32.250
and the kindest comment was that

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:34.960
it looke like dragged -out version of the
movie,

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:37.020
but with worse actors.

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:39.140
Touche, Ignacio!

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:40.180
This new show worries me,

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:43.730
and not because Terry Gilliam's time-travel
flick is sacrosanct.

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:46.780
Frankly,I think Gilliam's a heretic

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:51.510
for turning the flawless 1962 film La Jetée

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:53.920
into 12 Monkeys in the first place!

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:59.250
12 Monkeys is yet another time slot filled
by a lazy concept.

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:00.700
Flip around the dial tonight--

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:01.700
--ha!

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:02.700
dials...

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:05.199
--and you'll see brand extensions, reboots,

00:01:05.199 --> 00:01:08.300
and spinoffs of old public-domain stories.

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:13.409
And 12 Monkeys is just the tip of the derivative-berg!

00:01:13.409 --> 00:01:14.840
There are pilots in development

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:16.340
for shows based on movies like

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:18.100
Westworld, Big,

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:19.869
Rush Hour,

00:01:19.869 --> 00:01:20.869
Scream,

00:01:20.869 --> 00:01:22.300
Marley &amp; Me,

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:23.320
and--

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:25.040
Real Genius!?

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:27.700
Lazlo would be furious.

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:29.420
Okay, okay,

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:31.090
I'll admit that TV adaptations

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:33.030
of the movies Fargo, and

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:35.460
Alien Nation and Buffy worked well,

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:38.820
but these new do-overs are far more likely

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:40.040
to turn out like--

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:41.340
blech!--

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:42.420
Anger Management.

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:45.560
See, we remember the rare successes like MASH,

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:46.960
but we forget the

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:48.869
all-too-common dreck

00:01:48.869 --> 00:01:51.150
like the blessedly short-lived series

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:55.130
Ferris Bueller!

00:01:55.130 --> 00:02:01.399
“This is television--this is real.”

00:02:01.399 --> 00:02:02.710
Wouldn't the money sunk into

00:02:02.710 --> 00:02:04.440
licensing these old properties

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:06.840
be better spent on trying to create

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:09.909
y'know, something NEW ?

00:02:09.909 --> 00:02:10.970
I'm here to tell you that the

00:02:10.970 --> 00:02:13.049
Media Industry Human Centipede

00:02:13.049 --> 00:02:16.670
has officially begun eating its own tail.

00:02:16.670 --> 00:02:18.840
Hey, come to think of it,

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:21.099
why has no one made a series out of

00:02:21.099 --> 00:02:22.099
Human Centipede?

00:02:22.099 --> 00:02:23.469
Time to call my agent

00:02:23.469 --> 00:02:27.510
and set up a backdoor pilot!

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:30.400
Saturday morning cartoons came to an end last
fall,

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:33.500
but their spirit now seems to be inhabiting
prime time.

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:34.659
I mean, think about it--

00:02:34.659 --> 00:02:36.200
there were cartoons based on:

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:38.249
Free Willy, Ghostbusters,

00:02:38.249 --> 00:02:39.249
Beetlejuice,

00:02:39.249 --> 00:02:40.430
Karate Kid,

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:42.529
Bill &amp; Ted's Excellent Adventure,

00:02:42.529 --> 00:02:43.650
Back to the Future,

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:44.650
Beethoven,

00:02:44.650 --> 00:02:45.650
Mighty Ducks,

00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:46.650
The Mask,

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:47.650
Ace Ventura,

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:48.650
Men in Black,

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:49.650
Teen Wolf…

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:51.439
What TV show would YOU like to see turned
into a movie?

00:02:51.439 --> 00:02:52.609
Let me know in the comments,

00:02:52.609 --> 00:02:54.069
and subscribe to the WIRED channel.

00:02:54.069 --> 00:02:55.840
And be sure to watch the--

00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:56.840
Ahhhh!

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:57.989
Tiny versions of me!

00:02:57.989 --> 00:03:00.199
Stay back, mini-dopplegangers!

00:03:00.199 --> 00:03:02.680
Oh wait, those are links

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:04.079
to my other videos.

00:03:04.079 --> 00:03:05.730
Watch them all, they're great!

00:03:05.730 --> 00:03:07.839
Are they looking at me right now?

00:03:07.839 --> 00:03:09.899
I'm afraid to turn my head...

